[{"location":"reference/api/#API-Reference","page":"API Reference","title":"API Reference","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"reference/api/","page":"API Reference","title":"API Reference","text":"Modules = [JessamineSymbolics]\nOrder   = [:module, :constant, :type, :function, :macro,]","category":"page"},{"location":"reference/api/#JessamineSymbolics.DOTMAP","page":"API Reference","title":"JessamineSymbolics.DOTMAP","text":"DOTMAP\n\n(private) A mapping from standard functions to the symbols for their element-wise (dot) counterparts.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"constant"},{"location":"reference/api/#JessamineSymbolics.EPSILON","page":"API Reference","title":"JessamineSymbolics.EPSILON","text":"ε\n\nSpecial symbol used to handle problems with division by zero.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"constant"},{"location":"reference/api/#JessamineSymbolics.compile_to_function-Tuple{Jessamine.GenomeSpec, Jessamine.Agent}","page":"API Reference","title":"JessamineSymbolics.compile_to_function","text":"compile_to_function(g_spec::GenomeSpec, agent::Agent)\n\nCompile an agent to a function.  The returned value is a callable object that takes the x's as inputs and produces an output, using the parameter vector embedded in agent.  The function is compiled within the JessamineSymbolics module and should generally be used with dot broadcasting when called on inputs that are vectors.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"reference/api/#JessamineSymbolics.eval_time_step_symbolic-Tuple{Jessamine.GenomeSpec, Jessamine.Genome}","page":"API Reference","title":"JessamineSymbolics.eval_time_step_symbolic","text":"eval_time_step_symbolic(g_spec, genome; output_sym, scratch_sym, parameter_sym, input_sym)\n\nReturn symbolic objects representing a single time step of genome. The result is a named tuple with fields z, t, p, x for the Symbolics objects for those variables; c and c_next for the current and future cell state in symbolic form.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"reference/api/#JessamineSymbolics.insert_dot-Tuple{Any}","page":"API Reference","title":"JessamineSymbolics.insert_dot","text":"insert_dot(e)\n\n(private) Recursively traverses the expression e, replacing standard functions with the symbols for their element-wise (dot) counterparts according to DOTMAP.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"reference/api/#JessamineSymbolics.model_basic_symbolic_output-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"API Reference","title":"JessamineSymbolics.model_basic_symbolic_output","text":"model_basic_symbolic_output(g_spec, agent; kw_args...)\n\nBuild a Symbolics form for the output of the final time step of running agent's genome Then use the agent's parameter vector, and feed the symbolic output of the genome as input to model result in agent.extra to make a prediction in symbolic form.\n\nThe kw_args are eventually splatted into model_predict.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"reference/api/#JessamineSymbolics.model_basic_symbolic_output-Tuple{Jessamine.GenomeSpec, Jessamine.AbstractGenome, AbstractArray, Jessamine.AbstractModelResult}","page":"API Reference","title":"JessamineSymbolics.model_basic_symbolic_output","text":"model_basic_symbolic_output(g_spec, genome, parameter, model_result; kw_args...)\n\nBuild a Symbolics form for the output of the final time step of running genome Then use the parameter vector, the symbolic output of the genome, and feed the symbolic output of the genome as input to model result in agent.extra to make a prediction in symbolic form. No simplifications are performed.\n\nThe kw_args are eventually splatted into model_predict.\n\nReturn a named tuple with lots of useful fields.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"reference/api/#JessamineSymbolics.model_symbolic_output-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"API Reference","title":"JessamineSymbolics.model_symbolic_output","text":"model_symbolic_output(g_spec, agent; kw_args...)\n\nBuild a Symbolics form for the output of the final time step of running agent's genome Then use the agent's parameter vector, and feed the symbolic output of the genome as input to model result in agent.extra to make a prediction in symbolic form. The output tuple includes the result of various simplifications.\n\nThe kw_args are eventually splatted into model_predict.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"reference/api/#JessamineSymbolics.model_symbolic_output-Tuple{Jessamine.GenomeSpec, Jessamine.AbstractGenome, AbstractArray, Jessamine.AbstractModelResult}","page":"API Reference","title":"JessamineSymbolics.model_symbolic_output","text":"model_symbolic_output(g_spec, genome, parameter, model_result; kw_args...)\n\nBuild a Symbolics form for the output of the final time step of running genome Then use the parameter vector, the symbolic output of the genome, and feed the symbolic output of the genome as input to model result in agent.extra to make a prediction in symbolic form. The output tuple includes the result of various simplifications.\n\nThe kw_args are eventually splatted into model_predict.\n\nReturn a named tuple with lots of useful fields.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"reference/api/#JessamineSymbolics.replace_near_integer-Tuple{SymbolicUtils.BasicSymbolicImpl.var\"typeof(BasicSymbolicImpl)\"{T} where T}","page":"API Reference","title":"JessamineSymbolics.replace_near_integer","text":"replace_near_integer(expr; tolerance=1.0e-10)\n\nRound literal floating-point numbers within a symbolic expression. Specifically, if a number a differs round(a) by less thant tolerance, it gets replaced by round(a).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"reference/api/#JessamineSymbolics.run_genome_symbolic-Tuple{Jessamine.GenomeSpec, Jessamine.AbstractGenome}","page":"API Reference","title":"JessamineSymbolics.run_genome_symbolic","text":"run_genome_symbolic(g_spec, genome; parameter_sym=:p, input_sym=:x)\n\nBuild a symbolic form for the output of the final time step of running genome.  The parameter vector and input vector are Symbolics objects of the form p[j] and x[j].  The variable names can be specified with the keyword arguments.\n\nReturn a named tuple (p, x, z) where p and x, are vectors of Symbolics objects used to represent genome parameters and inputs; and z is a vector of genome outputs in symbolic form, equivalent to run_genome_to_last.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"reference/api/#JessamineSymbolics.show_symbolic-Tuple{Jessamine.GenomeSpec, Jessamine.Genome}","page":"API Reference","title":"JessamineSymbolics.show_symbolic","text":"show_symbolic(g_spec, genome; output_sym, scratch_sym, parameter_sym, input_sym)\n\nReturn a matrix with three columns. The first is row indices 1, 2, etc. The second is the initial workspace vector in symbolic form. The third is the future workspace state in symbolic form.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"reference/api/#JessamineSymbolics.symbolic_form-Tuple{Jessamine.GenomeSpec, Jessamine.Agent}","page":"API Reference","title":"JessamineSymbolics.symbolic_form","text":"symbolic_form(g_spec::GenomeSpec, agent::Agent)\n\nProduce a symbolic form for an agent.  Return a named tuple with field x equal to a symbol for the input array, and field vf equal to the outputs expressed in terms of x.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#JessamineSymbolics.jl","page":"JessamineSymbolics.jl","title":"JessamineSymbolics.jl","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"JessamineSymbolics.jl","title":"JessamineSymbolics.jl","text":"Documentation for JessamineSymbolics.jl","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"JessamineSymbolics.jl","title":"JessamineSymbolics.jl","text":"","category":"page"},{"location":"#Introduction","page":"JessamineSymbolics.jl","title":"Introduction","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"JessamineSymbolics.jl","title":"JessamineSymbolics.jl","text":"This package is an interface for using Jessamine.jl with Symbolics.jl","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"JessamineSymbolics.jl","title":"JessamineSymbolics.jl","text":"Note Jessamine is experimental and under development. Expect the source code to change in unpredictable ways.","category":"page"},{"location":"#Index","page":"JessamineSymbolics.jl","title":"Index","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"JessamineSymbolics.jl","title":"JessamineSymbolics.jl","text":"","category":"page"}]
